I recently ported Don G. Kneller's PC Hack 3.61 to PalmOS
powered devices running version 3.0 or higher. It is
available from my home page:

http://www.freewebs.com/drussell/

(on the Download page, the third entry in the
RevivedHack section)

History of this version
-----------------------

Hack by Jay Fenlason with help from Kenny Woodland, Mike
Thome and Jon Payne (inspired by Rogue; twice as many
monster types)
|
|--- Hack 1.0.3 by Andries E. Brouwer (greatly expanded;
     more than three times as large as the original)
     |
1986 |--- PC Hack 3.61 by Don G. Kneller (ported to MS-DOS,
          with many bugfixes)
          |
2004      |--- RevivedHack 1.1 by Donnie Russell
               (Windows/DOS/Linux port; color, bugfixes)
               |
2004           |--- rhp 1.1 by Donnie Russell
                    (PalmOS port; color, scrolling)

Note: In 1987, Hack became the basis for the modern game
NetHack.

